@startuml "Facade - Logging - Class Diagram"
skinparam classAttributeIconSize 0
hide empty members
title Facade — the one everybody has already used


class Application
interface Logger <<Facade>> {
  + info(message)
  + info(format, args...)
  + isInfoEnabled() : boolean
}
class LoggerFactory
class FacadeLogger

interface LoggingEngine <<subsystem>>
class ConsoleLoggingEngine
class JulLoggingEngine
class RecordingLoggingEngine

Application --> Logger
Logger <|.. FacadeLogger
LoggerFactory ..> FacadeLogger : creates
FacadeLogger o--> "1" LoggingEngine
LoggingEngine <|.. ConsoleLoggingEngine
LoggingEngine <|.. JulLoggingEngine
LoggingEngine <|.. RecordingLoggingEngine

note right of Logger
  Application code names <b>this</b>
  and nothing else.
end note

note bottom of LoggingEngine
  The backend is chosen <b>once</b>,
  at deployment — by somebody
  who is not the caller.
end note

note as N1
  isInfoEnabled() is on the facade for a
  reason: it lets the caller skip work the
  subsystem would only throw away.
end note

@enduml
